# "Ward abilities of those creatures don't trigger" (CR 702.21a): Bot2's Sedgemoor Witch has Ward - Pay 3 life. Bot1's Nowhere
# to Run kills Bot2's Ornithopter on turn three, and Bot1's Lightning Bolt aimed at the Witch (toughness 2) puts no ward ability
# on the stack: Bot1 is never asked to pay 3 life (the refusal), is still at 20 life, and the Witch dies. The Bolt would have
# been countered by a declined ward, as the sedgemoor-witch ward scenarios show.

[Bot1 Deck]
Swamp
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Nowhere to Run
Lightning Bolt
Island x14

[Bot2 Deck]
Forest
Mox Jet
Mox Emerald
Sedgemoor Witch
Ornithopter
Island x14

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot2.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Sedgemoor Witch.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Nowhere to Run.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Target(Ornithopter)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
! Bot1.Decline
Bot1.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot2.Battlefield.Sedgemoor Witch)
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Life = 20
Bot2.Graveyard = Ornithopter; Sedgemoor Witch
Bot1.Graveyard = Lightning Bolt
